/* SHABBAT SHEET (2026-11-04, Hanoch 1:02 to 1:25 PM): ONE addition, see RULES_DELTA.md.
NEW block settings/shabbatSheet: the weekly Shabbat sheet's changes for one
Shabbat (weeks) and its rows kept for every week (regular). Read: signed in
(the same as every settings document today; the public site does not show the
sheet). Create/update: whoever edits the screen today (hasScreen()), only the
keys weeks, regular, updatedBy, updatedAt (weeks: a map of at most 60 weeks,
regular: a list of at most 30 rows); delete never. Every other line is unchanged. */
/* 2040 PHASE 2 (2026-11-04, Hanoch 7:19 AM): ONE change, see RULES_DELTA.md.
NEW block settings/homeTexts: the landing page wording. Public read (the
landing page reads it signed out); create/update by the super admin only,
only the keys texts, textsEn, updatedBy, updatedAt (texts/textsEn maps of
at most 400 entries); delete never. Every other block is unchanged. */
/* STAGE 2 (2026-11-03): minimal delta over the live rules published
"Today 7:02 AM" on 2026-11-03 (see RULES_DELTA.md). Changes:
1. announcements, dedications, sponsors, flyers, yahrzeits: public read
   only when status is "published" (was: every document public). Content
   and Times gabbaim and the super admin read everything. Writes and
   deletes unchanged. No new collection.
2. REMOVED the two unused functions of the abolished read-only screen
   account (no rule called them: a no-op for access) and its wording
   in the comments. */
/* Firestore security rules, FIXED 2026-11-02: exists() guard before every get().data, so a missing users or congregants document returns false instead of a null
error, and a congregant without a users document can still read their own record. Based on the 2026-11-02 05:41 published rules, no other rule changed.
Purpose: enforce the append-only ledger in the database itself, not
only in the user interface. A user interface rule can be bypassed;
these rules cannot be bypassed by a normal client call.
Decisions enforced here (Hanoch, 2026-11-01 23:06, and critical
review 2026-11-01 23:11, foundation requirements):
- Security rules are a central design layer, not an extra
layer. Sensitive actions are verified server-side, in these
rules, not only in the user interface.
- A finance gabbai cannot edit his own permissions, and cannot
grant himself access. Only the super admin writes users.
- A screen gabbai cannot read finance data, in any collection.
- A congregant reads only the record whose email matches their
signed-in Google email, and reads only its ledger entries.
A congregant cannot change a balance, cannot write a ledger
entry, and cannot reach another congregant by changing an
address or an id in a request.
- Every financial action carries a unique operationId. The
operationIds collection allows create only when the id does
not already exist, and never allows update or delete, so a
duplicate submission is rejected in the database itself.
- Ledger entries can be created by authorized gabbaim and by the
super admin only. Ledger entries can NEVER be updated or deleted
by anyone, including the super admin and including gabbaim.
A mistake is fixed by a new correction entry with a signed
amount, never by editing or deleting the original entry.
- Finance backup is a day-one requirement, not a go-live item.
Backup exports read the full ledger and congregant records;
restore never deletes or overwrites existing entries (see
backup-design.md). Restore imports missing entries as new
entries with their original dates and entered-by values.
- The public TV page /tv/ uses no account: it reads only public
content (prayer times and published public screen items). The
screen device NEVER uses the super admin account.
- Super admin is hanochhason@gmail.com, management only. The
super admin chooses each gabbai's permissions: finance only,
content and times only, or both.
- A congregant signed in with Google using the email the super
admin added to their existing record reads ONLY their own
congregant record and its ledger entries, nothing else.
Roles are stored in users/{uid} documents, written by the super
admin only. A role document has: email and permissions (finance,
screen = content and times, or both). This draft assumes that shape; the exact
field names must be frozen when the Firebase project is created,
and the rules must be tested with test users before any real data
is imported. Do not deploy this draft to a project with real data
until those tests pass.
NOTE: this file is a draft for review. Firestore rules syntax must
be validated with the Firebase emulator or the Firebase console
rules tester before deployment. */

rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    function isSignedIn() {
      return request.auth != null;
    }
    function userDocExists() {
      return isSignedIn() && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid));
    }
    function userDoc() {
      return userDocExists() ? get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data : null;
    }
    function isSuperAdmin() {
      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.token.email == 'hanochhason@gmail.com';
    }
    /* Custom claims (option 2, transition: UID-doc checks are KEPT
    below, claims are added, not substituted, until migration
    is complete. See README.md, migration section. */
    function claimFinance() {
      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.token.ohFinance == true;
    }
    function claimScreen() {
      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.token.ohScreen == true;
    }
    function claimImageUpload() {
      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.token.ohImageUpload == true;
    }
    function hasFinance() {
      return isSuperAdmin() || claimFinance() || (userDocExists() && (userDoc().permissions == 'finance' || userDoc().permissions == 'both'));
    }
    function hasScreen() {
      return isSuperAdmin() || claimScreen() || (userDocExists() && (userDoc().permissions == 'screen' || userDoc().permissions == 'both'));
    }
    /* Stage D: the fields only the super admin writes on a congregant. */
    function stageDKeys() {
      return ['status', 'approvedBy', 'approvedAt', 'declinedBy', 'declinedAt', 'inactiveBy', 'inactiveAt', 'activeBy', 'activeAt'];
    }
    /* Stage D: finance adds members as before; a new record is active
    (no status, or status "active") and carries no stage D audit field. */
    function financeCreateOk() {
      return !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['approvedBy', 'approvedAt', 'declinedBy', 'declinedAt', 'inactiveBy', 'inactiveAt', 'activeBy', 'activeAt'])
        && (!('status' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.status == 'active');
    }

    /* Users and roles: super admin only writes. Nobody else can
    grant themselves finance or screen access. */
    match /users/{uid} {
      /* Email-read addition: a non-super-admin may read only a
      users doc whose email field equals their own token email.
      This is the same pattern already used for congregants.
      It does NOT list all users, and it does NOT grant finance
      or screen access by itself; hasFinance/hasScreen above
      still decide data access. */
      allow read: if isSuperAdmin() || request.auth.uid == uid || (isSignedIn() && resource.data.email == request.auth.token.email);
      allow create, update, delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }

    /* Idempotency: one operationId, one entry. Create only when
    the id is not already present. Update and delete denied
    for everyone, including the super admin. A duplicate
    submission with the same operationId must be rejected
    here, not only by disabling a button in the interface. */
    match /operationIds/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance();
      allow create: if hasFinance() && !exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/operationIds/$(id));
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    /* Pledges: a pledge is a commitment, not a charge and not a
    payment. Pledges are append only, like the ledger. A pledge
    becomes a charge only by a new ledger charge entry that
    references the pledge id; the pledge status change itself
    is recorded in the activity log, and past entries are never
    deleted. */
    match /pledges/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance();
      allow create: if hasFinance();
      allow update: if hasFinance() && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['status']);
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* Congregants: finance gabbaim and the super admin manage
    records. A congregant reads only their own record, by
    signed-in Google email. No congregant can list all records. */
    match /congregants/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance() || (isSignedIn() && resource.data.email == request.auth.token.email);
      /* Stage D (Hanoch 2026-11-04 4:12-4:14 PM): members and join requests.
      status: "pending" (a join request), "active" (or no status at all, as
      every record written before stage D), "declined", "inactive".
      Only the super admin approves, declines, makes inactive or active again
      (any write that touches status or the stage D audit fields). Finance
      keeps every write it had, except those fields. Nobody deletes. */
      allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin();
      allow create: if hasFinance() && financeCreateOk();
      allow update: if hasFinance() && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(stageDKeys());
      /* A signed-in person who is not a member yet sends ONE join request:
      document id "join_" + their own uid, their own verified sign-in email,
      only name + phone + email + status "pending" + createdAt, size caps.
      They cannot change it afterwards, cannot set a role (roles live in
      users/{uid} and custom claims, super admin only) and cannot read anyone
      else (the read rule above is unchanged). */
      allow create: if isSignedIn()
        && request.auth.token.email_verified == true
        && id == 'join_' + request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['name', 'phone', 'email', 'status', 'createdAt'])
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasAll(['name', 'phone', 'email', 'status', 'createdAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status == 'pending'
        && request.resource.data.email == request.auth.token.email
        && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() >= 2 && request.resource.data.name.size() <= 80
        && request.resource.data.phone is string && request.resource.data.phone.size() >= 7 && request.resource.data.phone.size() <= 30
        && request.resource.data.createdAt is string && request.resource.data.createdAt.size() <= 40;
      /* Stage D2 (Hanoch 2026-11-04 5:19 PM): a person whose request was
      declined may send it again. Only their own document join_<uid>, only
      from "declined" back to "pending", only name + phone + email + status +
      createdAt change (same shape and caps as the first request). The old
      declinedBy/declinedAt stay as they are. No role or approval field, no
      edit of a pending request, nothing on an active or inactive record. */
      allow update: if isSignedIn()
        && request.auth.token.email_verified == true
        && id == 'join_' + request.auth.uid
        && resource.data.status == 'declined'
        && request.resource.data.status == 'pending'
        && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['name', 'phone', 'email', 'status', 'createdAt'])
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['name', 'phone', 'email', 'status', 'createdAt', 'declinedBy', 'declinedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.email == request.auth.token.email
        && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() >= 2 && request.resource.data.name.size() <= 80
        && request.resource.data.phone is string && request.resource.data.phone.size() >= 7 && request.resource.data.phone.size() <= 30
        && request.resource.data.createdAt is string && request.resource.data.createdAt.size() <= 40;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* Ledger entries: APPEND ONLY. Finance gabbaim and the
    super admin create. Nobody updates or deletes. A
    congregant reads only their own entries. */
    match /ledgerEntries/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance() || (isSignedIn() && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/congregants/$(resource.data.congregantId)) && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/congregants/$(resource.data.congregantId)).data.email == request.auth.token.email);
      allow create: if hasFinance();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    /* Nedarim: finance only, append only. */
    match /nedarim/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance();
      allow create: if hasFinance();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    /* Recurring schedules: finance only. Schedules are
    templates; actual charges are ledger entries. */
    match /recurringSchedules/{id} {
      allow read: if hasFinance();
      allow create, update: if hasFinance();
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* Activity log: internal audit. Finance, screen and super
    admin read and create; nobody updates or deletes. */
    match /activityLog/{id} {
      allow read: if isSuperAdmin() || hasFinance() || hasScreen();
      allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || hasFinance() || hasScreen();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    /* Screen content: public read. Screen gabbaim and the
    super admin edit and delete (stage B1, Hanoch 2026-11-03:
    content gabbaim manage prayer times fully). hasScreen()
    already includes the super admin. */
    match /prayerTimes/{docId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if hasScreen();
    }
    /* Stage 2: the content editor writes announcements, dedications,
    sponsors, flyers and yahrzeits. The public (/tv/, no sign-in) reads
    only documents with status "published"; drafts and archived items
    are read by Content and Times gabbaim and the super admin only.
    Writes and deletes are unchanged. */
    match /announcements/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.get('status', '') == 'published' || hasScreen();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }
    match /dedications/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.get('status', '') == 'published' || hasScreen();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }
    match /sponsors/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.get('status', '') == 'published' || hasScreen();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }
    match /flyers/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.get('status', '') == 'published' || hasScreen();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }
    match /yahrzeits/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.get('status', '') == 'published' || hasScreen();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen();
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
    }

    /* Settings: signed-in read; super admin only writes. */
    match /settings/{docId} {
      allow read: if isSignedIn();
      allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin();
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* 2040 phase 1 (Hanoch 2026-11-04, 5:29 to 5:51 AM: every word on the
    screen easy to edit, Hebrew and English, and the order of the blocks): the
    TV wording and arrangement. Only public screen wording, no private data, so
    the TV reads it with no sign-in. Content gabbaim and the super admin write
    it, with only these keys (texts, textsEn, layout: maps of at most 400
    entries each). Firestore ORs the matches: the settings block above is unchanged. */
    match /settings/screenTexts {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create, update: if hasScreen()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['texts', 'textsEn', 'layout', 'updatedBy', 'updatedAt'])
        && (!('texts' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.texts is map && request.resource.data.texts.size() <= 400))
        && (!('textsEn' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.textsEn is map && request.resource.data.textsEn.size() <= 400))
        && (!('layout' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.layout is map && request.resource.data.layout.size() <= 400));
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* 2040 phase 2 (Hanoch 2026-11-04 7:19 AM): the landing page wording, edited
    by the super admin only. Only public landing page words, no private data, so
    the landing page reads it with no sign-in. Exactly these keys (texts,
    textsEn: maps of at most 400 entries). Firestore ORs the matches: the
    settings block above is unchanged. */
    match /settings/homeTexts {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['texts', 'textsEn', 'updatedBy', 'updatedAt'])
        && (!('texts' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.texts is map && request.resource.data.texts.size() <= 400))
        && (!('textsEn' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.textsEn is map && request.resource.data.textsEn.size() <= 400));
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* Shabbat sheet (Hanoch 2026-11-04 1:02 to 1:25 PM): this Shabbat's changes to
    the printed sheet (weeks: { "YYYY-MM-DD": {times, hidden, star, extra} }) and
    the rows kept for every week (regular). Only Shabbat times and row names, no
    private data. Written by whoever edits the screen today (hasScreen(), the
    same writers as settings/screenTexts), exactly these keys, size caps.
    Firestore ORs the matches: the settings block above is unchanged. */
    match /settings/shabbatSheet {
      allow read: if isSignedIn();
      allow create, update: if hasScreen()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['weeks', 'regular', 'updatedBy', 'updatedAt'])
        && (!('weeks' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.weeks is map && request.resource.data.weeks.size() <= 60))
        && (!('regular' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.regular is list && request.resource.data.regular.size() <= 30))
        && (!('updatedBy' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.updatedBy is string && request.resource.data.updatedBy.size() <= 200));
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    /* Everything else: deny by default. */
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
